--- !u!114 &1744216724
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1744216722}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 7b30be7afae079b499303176a7d752e6, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  characterName: Soldier
  style1:
  - '"Do you know who I am?" You repeat when they just stare at you.'
  - Their hair waves oddly, and to your complete confusion, they incline their head.
    "I apologize for any offense I have caused."
  - That... isn't helpful. You frown and again repeat your question, and the alien
    soldier's hair raises and sort of trembles and they apologize again and then
    scamper away before you can try asking another way.
  - You gleaned nothing from that interaction, except that their species is either
    meek or yours is fearsome.
  - You don't... feel particularly fearsome? Hm.
  style2:
  - '"The same place we have been going for far too long," they say, long hair raising
    as if in a breeze.'
  - '"That''s not really an answer," you blurt.'
  - Their hair begins to wave and flutter. "Our fool of a navigator claims the ship's
    system malfunctioned a decade ago, so we went the opposite direction to the one
    we should have," they say tersely. "If the diplomat we are escorting were not
    of such a long-lived species, we may well have caused a war by now."
  - '"...but where are we going?" You press.'
  - Their hair splays behind them dramatically. "To --."
  - You blink at them and decide you physically cannot pronounce the odd sound they
    just made, and the soldier alien elects to take their leave, hair waving gently
    in their wake.
  style3:
  - You decide to play it safe and make small talk, unwilling to alert them to the
    fact that you may be an intruder.
  - The crew member, it seems, is having a spat with the lead engineer, who insists
    the climate control is set to be comfortable for all species aboard the ship,
    nevermind that the alien you're speaking to holds up their arm to show you their...
    uh... prickly hairs?
  - '"My species does not grow hair," they hiss. "I am reverting to an archaic adaptation
    because this ship is entirely too frigid!" The glare back at the long hair waving
    in a nonexistent breeze behind them.'
  - You look between the small hairs and the livid face. "Have you... tried wearing
    a jacket?"
  - An annoyed snarl, and they abruptly turn down a hall and vanish, the long hair
    atop their head flowing in their wake and apparently done with this conversation.
  - Well then.
  style4:
  - "The crew member eventually whirls to face you, hair waving erratically. \u201CWhat
    do you want, fool?\u201D"
  - "You freeze. \u201CI\u2026 just, uh\u2026 am going where you\u2019re going?\u201D"
  - "\u201CI am going to my personal quarters,\u201D the soldier-esque alien hisses.
    \u201CI have already spent far too long on what should have been a simple mission
    because our navigator is more fool than you are, so begone.\u201D"
  - You scamper away lest your so far very short life end early.
  style5:
  - "It\u2019s instinct, really, something about the soldier uniform, maybe, but
    you\u2019re still reeling from whatever took your memories, and they\u2019re
    unfortunately skilled, and you find yourself on your behind on the metal floor
    entirely too quickly."
  - "\u201CIf you wish to spar, you are supposed to request it, and do so in the
    training hall,\u201D the alien says coolly, arms crossed. \u201CI recognize no
    one has defeated me in several years now, but even so, this tactic is cowardly
    and foolish, so I suggest you stay out of my sight for the next several years
    lest I decided to spar with you properly.\u201D"
  - "A sharp smile, and they take their leave, and you idly decide you narrowly avoided
    death, and most likely by being so incompetent they didn\u2019t see you as a
    threat, which is kind of insulting even if you are still feeling a little lightheaded."
  flavors:
  - Ask them who you are.
  - Ask them where the ship is going.
  - Make small talk.
  - Follow them silently, uncertain as to what to say.
  - Try to knock them out.
  pretext:
  - You trot to catch up to the soldier.
  - Thankfully, they speak your language, albeit a bit stiffly.
  points: 0a0000000a0000000a0000000a0000000a000000
