--- !u!114 &1873029211
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1873029209}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 7b30be7afae079b499303176a7d752e6, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  characterName: Snob
  style1:
  - "A large eye blinks at you, and antennae wave curiously. \u201CThis is being
    moved from the lab to the storage room,\u201D the alien says, voice monotone.
    \u201CWe are still researching it; I cannot give it away.\u201D"
  - "\u201CIsn\u2019t it just a bracelet?\u201D You try with a charming smile."
  - "\u201CNegative,\u201D the alien says, facing forward once more. \u201CIt has
    a strange energy we cannot place, and we have enough time remaining on our journey
    to discover the mysteries it contains.\u201D What may be a smile. \u201CIf I
    had not had this to study all these years, I may well have made a snack out of
    our incompetent navigator.\u201D"
  - You elect to make idle chitchat after that lest this crew member make a snack
    of you, though you at least learn the bracelet is being kept in the storage bay.
  style2:
  - "An aggrieved gasp. \u201CI do not judge items by aesthetics but by functionality,\u201D
    the alien says, clearly indignant. The box is held aloft, and a reverent, one-eyed
    gaze fixes on the item inside. \u201CI have yet to discover this accessory\u2019s
    purpose, but the energy readings I have gotten\u2026 ohh\u2026\u201D A full-body
    shiver."
  - "This alien is very attached to your bracelet, and also breathing oddly now and
    cradling the box close like a lover, and you keep walking beside them and doing
    your best not to comment on it until they reach the storage bay, drawling you
    don\u2019t have access and shutting the door in your face."
  - What a lovely personality.
  style3:
  - "A dreamy sigh, and a clawed hand stroking the clear box your bracelet is in.
    \u201CI have spent seven day cycles studying this lovely relic, and sadly must
    sleep for three now,\u201D the alien says, voice forlorn and antennae drooping.
    \u201COh, what I could discover if only I could go longer without recharge. Woe
    am I, to be born to a warrior species!\u201D"
  - "The crew member complains so much you can\u2019t really get a word in after
    that, but they wave goodbye to you before going into the storage bay to secure
    the bracelet, which you now know will be there for a few days, so you consider
    the interaction a success."
  style4:
  - "The alien doesn\u2019t notice you trailing after them, too fixated on the bracelet
    within the box and overtly shielding it from even those walking close to the
    opposite wall in the wide hallways, occasionally hissing as they do."
  - "You peek around a corner and see them vanish into a storage bay, and when they
    leave empty-handed you pray to whatever divinity will listen that they\u2019ll
    be gone awhile."
  style5:
  - You fail, because of course you do, your gaze so desperately fixated on the box
    that you fail to realize just how many legs its holder has, and you trip over
    them and go sprawling on the floor, the alien none the wiser.
  - "Just as you climb to your feet, swaying and mumbling curses, you see a crew
    member in what must be the ship\u2019s soldier uniform brush against the alien
    with the box, and then they\u2019re quickly dodging when a spiked tail lunges
    at them."
  - "\u201CYou fool,\u201D the alien hisses, cradling the box with your bracelet
    close and the soldier already scurrying back and muttering about testy scientists.
    \u201CWhat if I had dropped this mysterious relic? I have not even discovered
    its secrets yet and you\u2026 you\u2026\u201D"
  - "The soldier wisely flees, a strange purple cloud appearing around the alien,
    and a second later the ship isolates them with clear barriers as the air is cleaned,
    the scientist sighing and stroking the box, mumbling to in a language you don\u2019t
    know as the ship cleans what the barriers are warning is \u2018lethal poison
    mist\u2019."
  - You elect to follow from afar after that, relieved to see the alien who for some
    reason became a scientist instead of an elite soldier leaving the bracelet in
    the storage bay.
  flavors:
  - Catch up and ask for the bracelet.
  - Race up and ask what's with the ugly bracelet.
  - Match their pace and ask how their simulated day cycle has been.
  - Follow them quietly, uncertain as to what to do.
  - Try to snatch the bracelet.
  pretext:
  - You close in on the crew member.
  points: 0a0000000a0000000a0000000a0000000a000000
